      "has_readme": true,
      "readme_length": 3771,
      "readme_excerpt": "#  YC Startup App\n\nA modern startup directory application built with Next.js, Sanity CMS, and NextAuth. Users can create profiles, upload photos, and share their startup ideas.\n\n##  Features\n\n- 🔐 **GitHub OAuth Authentication** - Secure login with NextAuth.js\n- 👤 **User Profiles** - Custom profile photos and bio management\n- 🏢 **Startup Management** - Create, view, and manage startup listings\n- 🎨 **Modern Design** - Pink-themed UI with responsive design\n- 📱 **Mobile Friendly** - Optimized for all device sizes\n- 🔍 **Search & Filter** - Find startups by category or keywords\n- 📊 **Content Management** - Multiple options for managing content\n\n## 🛠️ Tech Stack\n\n- **Frontend**: Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS, Custom CSS\n- **Authentication**: NextAuth.js v5\n- **CMS**: Sanity.io\n- **Database**: Sanity (NoSQL)\n- **Deployment**: Vercel (recommended)\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Node.js 18+ \n- npm or yarn\n- Sanity account\n- GitHub OAuth app\n\n### Installation\n\n1. **Clone the repository**\n   ```bash\n   git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/yc-startup-app.git\n   cd yc-startup-app\n   ```\n\n2. **Install dependencies**\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n",
